---
// A docs guide page in phase 16's shape: prose, a numbered procedure, code blocks labeled with their
// file, a real specimen breaking out of the text column, a callout, and previous and next links.
import Specimen from '../../components/Specimen.astro'
import Docs from './_Docs.astro'
import { wireframe } from './_nav'

const manifest = `"contributions": {
  "frames": [{
    "target": "pane", "id": "issues", "label": "Issues",
    "layout": "single",
    "regions": { "body": { "kind": "remote", "entry": "pane" } }
  }]
}`
const client = `const tree = el('ListDetail', { split: true }, [
  el('ListColumn', { label: 'Issues' }, rows),
  el('DetailColumn', {}, [el('Heading', {}, [text(selected.title)])]),
])`
---

<Docs
  title="Add a pane"
  section="build"
  toc={['Before you start', 'Add the manifest entry', 'Draw the tree', 'Mistakes', 'Limits', 'Reference']}
>
  <p>Add a pane to a task's row, drawn from your plugin's tree, in the desktop app and the terminal client.</p>
  <div class="breakout">
    <Specimen id="list-detail" />
  </div>
  <aside class="callout" id="before-you-start">
    <b>Before you start</b>
    <p>Build the plugin in <a href={wireframe('tutorial')}>Build your first plugin</a>. This guide adds to it.</p>
  </aside>
  <h2 id="add-the-manifest-entry">Add the manifest entry</h2>
  <p>A pane is a frame with the pane target. The host draws the pane's box, and your tree fills its one region.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <p>Add a frame to the contributions in your manifest.</p>
      <div class="code">
        <div><span>acorn-plugin.json</span><span>Copy</span></div>
        <pre set:text={manifest} />
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>Reload the plugin. The pane shows in the task's pane switcher.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id="draw-the-tree">Draw the tree</h2>
  <ol class="steps" start="3">
    <li>
      <p>Build the pane's tree in your client entry.</p>
      <div class="code">
        <div><span>client.js</span><span>Copy</span></div>
        <pre set:text={client} />
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>Open the pane, then open the same task in the terminal client. Both draw the list and the detail.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id="mistakes">Mistakes</h2>
  <div class="cols breakout" style="--min: 280px">
    <div class="code">
      <div><span>Wrong: acorn-plugin.json</span></div>
      <pre set:text={'"layout": "single", "regions": { "list": … }'} />
    </div>
    <div class="code">
      <div><span>Right: acorn-plugin.json</span></div>
      <pre set:text={'"layout": "single", "regions": { "body": … }'} />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>The single layout has one region, body. Draft: phase 16 takes each mistake from the Node's refusal messages.</p>
  <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
  <p>A draft list of the caps on panes per plugin, and what the terminal client draws one pane at a time.</p>
  <h2 id="reference">Reference</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#">Contributions: frames</a></li>
    <li><a href="#">Layouts</a></li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
